      "content": "This unpredictable behavior often aligns with exceeding the material's glass transition or viscoelastic threshold within the friction layer. When the rapid thermal gradients create localized points where the binder or matrix starts to soften or deform microscopically, the surface energy and contact pressure become unstable. This transition causes rapid, non-linear changes in the coefficient of friction, which the driver perceives as an erratic or \"mischievous\" feel, even before bulk fade occurs.",
